{"format":"edusim-world","version":1,"exportedAt":"2026-08-17T04:49:51.515Z","records":[{"id":"18f014f6-6afb-471a-90fc-da564cf5e224","kind":"world-theme","theme":"colosseum","createdAt":1786942191439,"transform":{"position":[0,0,0],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]}},{"id":"50036399-44c9-41d9-b5f2-2c84f92e2f02","kind":"world-spawn","createdAt":1786942191439,"transform":{"position":[62,0,150],"rotation":[0,0.3919475254685127,0],"scale":[1,1,1]}},{"id":"4962c6a1-242f-44f6-b355-8a606730a574","createdAt":1786942191441,"transform":{"position":[0,0,0],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"colosseum","options":{"radiusX":100,"radiusZ":82,"height":50,"bays":80,"ruinFrom":0.02,"ruinTo":0.52,"seed":5}},{"id":"01d2f0f5-f0b2-4312-8bff-9d7fcc05fe18","createdAt":1786942191443,"transform":{"position":[0,0,0],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"hypogeum","options":{"radiusX":47,"radiusZ":29,"deck":0.42,"seed":11}},{"id":"ed5a8a2d-7f50-4e7d-92d1-006d04738a8c","createdAt":1786942191446,"transform":{"position":[52,0.33735921845009864,118],"rotation":[0,0.3028848683749714,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Built here at a third of full size","title":"The Colosseum","accent":"#a8834a","body":"The real one is 615ft by 510ft and 157ft tall — bigger than this whole world, which is why it is built smaller here. Eighty arches ring the ground floor and they were numbered: your pottery ticket gave you a gate, a stair and a row, and fifty thousand people could clear the building in minutes. Modern stadiums still use the plan."}},{"id":"44989a78-6913-48a7-84fb-616434aa8d1f","createdAt":1786942191448,"transform":{"position":[-58,0.2291210783455533,112],"rotation":[0,1.264120007393214,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Two thirds of it is missing","title":"Where the rest went","accent":"#8c7a56","body":"It was not destroyed in a war. Earthquakes brought down the south side, and then for a thousand years Rome quarried it — the travertine went into palaces, bridges and St Peter's. What you can see of the outer wall is the piece nobody got round to taking. The holes all over it are where iron cramps were levered out."}},{"id":"b17584d9-2938-4253-9d0e-37b94b70296a","createdAt":1786942191449,"transform":{"position":[20,-0.1518207144367576,-104],"rotation":[0,-0.18998828791871572,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Under the floor","title":"The hypogeum","accent":"#9c6a4e","body":"The arena floor is gone, so you can see the two storeys of tunnels underneath it. Thirty-two lifts worked by counterweight brought animals and scenery straight up into the arena through trapdoors. The wooden deck at one end is a modern reconstruction, put there so people can see how high the floor was."}},{"id":"31f42a6c-579e-4825-abbe-36fb56113248","createdAt":1786942191450,"transform":{"position":[118,0.07483449659781671,62],"rotation":[0,-0.5667292175235064,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"arch-of-constantine","options":{"width":34,"height":27,"depth":10,"seed":7}},{"id":"611047b9-3752-4bfa-828b-94d02cb3f626","createdAt":1786942191451,"transform":{"position":[104,0.11666604114742718,88],"rotation":[0,-0.5954098754787326,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Second-hand sculpture","title":"The Arch of Constantine","accent":"#8a7f6c","body":"Put up in 315 AD, and most of the carving on it is older than the arch: roundels from a monument of Hadrian's, panels from Marcus Aurelius, statues from Trajan. Faces were recut to look like Constantine. Historians argue about whether that was thrift, hurry, or a deliberate claim to stand in a line of good emperors."}},{"id":"bf2086bb-dc17-4232-8fe0-b1ea177bc1bb","createdAt":1786942191452,"transform":{"position":[-128,0.3207176736086761,34],"rotation":[0,0.35,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"forum-columns","options":{"count":6,"height":26,"spacing":9,"seed":17}},{"id":"6ae2a7c7-2477-48c2-81ab-41d3943e1f0c","createdAt":1786942191454,"transform":{"position":[-142,0.3774443031077146,-28],"rotation":[0,1.2,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"forum-columns","options":{"count":4,"height":21,"spacing":8,"entablature":false,"seed":23}},{"id":"132cd3e6-1e9b-4a2e-9a80-e93f448b6e74","createdAt":1786942191455,"transform":{"position":[-104,-0.20997457462681535,76],"rotation":[0,1.1514546792448668,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"she-wolf-column","options":{"height":13,"seed":21}},{"id":"ce5857c4-3473-4ba6-a224-b0707bd95283","createdAt":1786942191456,"transform":{"position":[-96,-0.16691755087872817,60],"rotation":[0,1.05301446818221,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"The city's own founding story","title":"The she-wolf","accent":"#5c6b4a","body":"Rome said it was founded by twins raised by a wolf. Romulus killed Remus in an argument over where the walls should go, and named the city after himself. Romans knew it was a legend and told it anyway — it says the place was built by outcasts and settled by force, which is closer to the truth than most founding stories manage."}},{"id":"847e60bf-eb81-42eb-8b8b-bc5ed2c6c5b1","createdAt":1786942191457,"transform":{"position":[-16,-1.7763568394002505e-15,8],"rotation":[0,0.4,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"gladiator","options":{"height":5.6,"tunic":11553338,"seed":3}},{"id":"291ed6a7-71b2-48ad-8684-a5415299e62a","createdAt":1786942191459,"transform":{"position":[8,2.6645352591003757e-15,-12],"rotation":[0,3.5,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"gladiator","options":{"height":5.6,"tunic":4156298,"seed":9}},{"id":"b465a05d-8aa6-4607-b2f4-37217b206933","createdAt":1786942191460,"transform":{"position":[122,0.26895215474748646,40],"rotation":[0,-0.49934672168013006,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"gladiator","options":{"height":5.6,"tunic":9071167,"seed":15}},{"id":"181f64e2-3abe-4e11-a851-ccc2f8218b7a","createdAt":1786942191461,"transform":{"position":[-34,-4.884981308350689e-15,22],"rotation":[0,1.0838970949836275,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Mostly they did not die","title":"Gladiators","accent":"#8c4a3a","body":"A trained gladiator was expensive — years of feeding, coaching and doctoring — so the owner who lent him out wanted him back. Fights were refereed, and most ended with a surrender. Some were free men who volunteered for the money. Most were slaves or prisoners, and none of that was their choice."}},{"id":"cbd80f10-16e6-4d9d-b0ca-d415931df4d5","createdAt":1786942191462,"transform":{"position":[-152,-0.7688332399298474,96],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"stone-pine","options":{"height":36,"seed":200}},{"id":"e14bce55-2bc0-4ceb-a0ca-0b05967d912a","createdAt":1786942191464,"transform":{"position":[-118,-0.3272549915570835,128],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"stone-pine","options":{"height":32,"seed":207}},{"id":"d79f2d18-22f2-45de-8088-212749cddc8f","createdAt":1786942191465,"transform":{"position":[136,-0.7992782405355334,118],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"stone-pine","options":{"height":34,"seed":214}},{"id":"65e20c79-8eb4-4fd5-bd67-652859a5d3cb","createdAt":1786942191466,"transform":{"position":[162,-0.5041907396834682,74],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"stone-pine","options":{"height":30,"seed":221}},{"id":"d35f82ac-95cd-4ec6-b6f8-18ca7d2374de","createdAt":1786942191467,"transform":{"position":[-166,-0.011928005531982144,-44],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"stone-pine","options":{"height":33,"seed":228}},{"id":"8a35f808-7904-402f-b21a-6a23ae1d9f4f","createdAt":1786942191469,"transform":{"position":[-138,0.1593523712